DATE Operations

The first operation we should learn is:

DATEDIFF()
---------------------------------------------

It is used to calculate the difference between two dates.

Basic idea
DATEDIFF(date1, date2)

It returns the number of days between the two dates.

For example:

SELECT DATEDIFF('2024-01-10', '2024-01-01');

Result:

9

Because:

Jan 1 → Jan 10 = 9 days
Important ⚠️

The order matters:

DATEDIFF('2024-01-10', '2024-01-01')

→ 9

But:

DATEDIFF('2024-01-01', '2024-01-10')

→ -9

So remember:

DATEDIFF(later_date, earlier_date)
              ↓
        positive days
Using your employee table

We can calculate how many days have passed between an employee's joining date and today:

SELECT emp_name, joining_date,
       DATEDIFF(CURDATE(), joining_date) AS days_worked
FROM employees;

Conceptually:

Today
  ↓
2026-10-03
  -
Joining date
  ↓
2023-06-12
  =
Number of days

AS days_worked is just giving the calculated column a readable name.

🧠 Remember
DATEDIFF()
     ↓
Difference between two dates
     ↓
Result is in DAYS
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATE_ADD()
--------------------------------------------------

DATE_ADD() is used when you want to add a specific amount of time to a date.

Basic syntax
DATE_ADD(date, INTERVAL value unit)

For example:

SELECT DATE_ADD('2024-01-10', INTERVAL 10 DAY);

Result:

2024-01-20

Because:

2024-01-10
     + 10 days
     ↓
2024-01-20
You can add different units
Add days
DATE_ADD('2024-01-10', INTERVAL 10 DAY)
Add months
DATE_ADD('2024-01-10', INTERVAL 2 MONTH)

Result:

2024-03-10
Add years
DATE_ADD('2024-01-10', INTERVAL 1 YEAR)

Result:

2025-01-10

So the pattern is:

DATE_ADD
   ↓
date
   ↓
INTERVAL
   ↓
amount
   ↓
DAY / MONTH / YEAR
🔥 Using your employee table

Suppose ANU joined on:

2023-06-12

We can calculate the date 6 months after joining:

SELECT DATE_ADD(joining_date, INTERVAL 6 MONTH)
FROM employees
WHERE emp_name = 'ANU';

Result:

2023-12-12
🧠 Easy memory trick
DATEDIFF()  → Find difference
DATE_ADD()  → Add time
