---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATE_SUB() 📅

It does the reverse of DATE_ADD():

DATE_ADD() → moves date forward
DATE_SUB() → moves date backward

Example:

SELECT DATE_SUB('2024-01-10', INTERVAL 2 MONTH);

Result:

2023-11-10
-------------------------------------------------------------------
 Chain DATE_ADD() / DATE_SUB()

Suppose:

2024-01-10

You want to add 1 year + 2 months + 10 days:
SELECT DATE_ADD(
         DATE_ADD(
           DATE_ADD('2024-01-10', INTERVAL 1 YEAR),
           INTERVAL 2 MONTH
         ),
         INTERVAL 10 DAY
       );

Result:

2025-03-20

Because:

2024-01-10
+ 1 year  → 2025-01-10
+ 2 months → 2025-03-10
+ 10 days → 2025-03-20
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
